// references/playbill.md, generated by tools/assets.mjs: how the RH of the cast reads the facts — what each situation
// means, the words of a post, and which findings make a development plan. Never edit the generated file by hand.
import { PDI_GROUPS } from './pdi'
import { REQUIREMENTS } from './playbill'

const GROUPS: Record<string, string> = {
  contradictions: 'what was declared against the YAML; a rule that confronts the text with the setup',
  contract: 'the inputs the orchestrator does not pass in one call (one item), a short routing description, a flow that returns nothing; a call to one not in the folder is the orchestrator’s',
  off: 'off a pattern, one item per fact, a variation of an official block included',
  rules: 'a rule of the profile not met',
  text: 'a marker set twice in one',
  telemetry: 'an event spelt another way, a field missing, an event that did not fire, no line in the telemetry, no telemetry',
  cleanup: 'what nobody uses or is switched off — it does not put anyone in a plan alone',
}

export function playbillMarkdown(): string {
  return `# The RH of the cast (--playbill)

Generated from \`dev/agent-review/src/\`. The same cast, as people. Nothing is guessed: a field nothing says is left empty.

## The staff board

| Situation | When |
|---|---|
| on the staff | in the folder |
| being hired | called by the orchestrator and not in the folder, or in an environment (\`declared:environment\`) not the one most are in |
| with no owner | no \`declared:owner\` (the inventory's Owner) — only with the inventory |
| never published | a row in the inventory and no \`declared:last-published\` — only with the inventory |
| with no evaluation | no export of the Evaluate tab names it — only with \`--evals\` |
| with a development plan | one item of the plan or more that is not cleanup |
| in good standing | no item, or only cleanup |

## The résumé

The title is the first sentence of the instructions, as written; the summary, their first list (at most 5). The team is
\`declared:team\` (the team spreadsheet's «Dono»), the owner \`declared:owner\`, the goal \`declared:kpi\`. The performance
comes from \`--telemetry\`: topic starts (\`TopicStart\`), errors logged (the events of its YAML that fired) and those that
did not fire. The goal is never measured from the telemetry.

## Certifications (--evals)

\`--evals <folder>\` reads the exports of Copilot Studio's Evaluate tab, «Evaluate <name> <date>.csv»: who is named by
the file, a row passes when every \`result_N\` says Pass, and each method (\`testMethodType_N\`) is counted. Only the
counts are kept: \`question\`, \`expectedResponse\`, \`actualResponse\` and \`explanation_N\` are the client's
conversation and never reach an output. Who has one gets the fact \`eval:run\`, so a rule \`has: "eval:*"\` asks every
one of a role for it. A file that names nobody in the folder, or has no \`result_1\`, is told and left out.

## The review of access

Within each type of two or more, a connector, an MCP server or what a flow reaches that only one has is asked about on
the résumé and on the stage's card: does the post need it? It becomes a cleanup item of the plan only when the team
decides so — a decision \`rejected\` on that key, in the type's scope (\`type:<id>\`).

## The post

The accepted patterns of the role or type and the profile's rules (\`has\`); with no decision yet, the patterns someone is
off, as a proposal. A fact with no words below is «Has «…»».

| Key | Requirement (en) | Requirement (pt) |
|---|---|---|
${Object.entries(REQUIREMENTS).map(([k, v]) => `| \`${k}\` | ${v.en} | ${v.pt} |`).join('\n')}

## The development plan

What «to look at» says about one alone, written as an action, one item per fact, in this order:

${PDI_GROUPS.map((g, i) => `${i + 1}. **${g}** — ${GROUPS[g]}.`).join('\n')}

Not in anyone's plan: what only one has (innovation or debt is the team's call), a type with one specialist, a marker
set in different ways across the cast, what was not understood, and what a decision rejected.
`
}
